  "details": "- nfs: fix possible null-ptr-deref when parsing param {CVE-2022-50455}\n- KVM: arm64: Disassociate vcpus from redistributor region on teardown {CVE-2024-40989}\n- HID: core: Harden s32ton() against conversion to 0 bits {CVE-2025-38556}\n- ALSA: usb-audio: Validate UAC3 cluster segment descriptors {CVE-2025-39757}\n- tcp_bpf: Fix the sk_mem_uncharge logic in tcp_bpf_sendmsg {CVE-2024-56633}\n- ovl: Filter invalid inodes with missing lookup function {CVE-2024-56570}\n- ACPI: processor: Check for null return of devm_kzalloc() in fch_misc_setup() {CVE-2023-53483}\n- crypto: seqiv - Handle EBUSY correctly {CVE-2023-53373}\n- KVM: nSVM: Check instead of asserting on nested TSC scaling support {CVE-2023-53663}\n- ice: Don't tx before switchdev is fully configured {CVE-2023-53657}\n- rcu: Avoid stack overflow due to __rcu_irq_enter_check_tick() being kprobe-ed {CVE-2023-53655}\n- mm/swap: fix swap_info_struct race between swapoff and get_swap_pages() {CVE-2023-53623}\n- ext4: fix bug_on in __es_tree_search caused by bad boot loader inode {CVE-2022-50485}\n- ext4: add EXT4_IGET_BAD flag to prevent unexpected bad inode {CVE-2022-50485}\n- ext4: add helper to check quota inums {CVE-2022-50485}\n- ext4: fix bug_on in __es_tree_search caused by bad quota inode {CVE-2022-50485}\n- swiotlb: Fix double-allocation of slots due to broken alignment handling {CVE-2024-35814}\n- swiotlb: fix a braino in the alignment check fix {CVE-2024-35814}\n- swiotlb: fix slot alignment checks {CVE-2024-35814}\n- swiotlb: fix the deadlock in swiotlb_do_find_slots\n- drm/radeon: free iio for atombios when driver shutdown {CVE-2023-53453}",
